  narrativeGranted: "She still lives with her parents, a fact she doesn\u2019t mention
    whenever making small talk. She justifies it by saying she is helping take care
    of her little sister, Mia. If you ask Mia, the best thing about having her sister
    at home is that she leaves weed in the top drawer of the dresser and never notices
    when the supply goes down. Mackenzie pays her share in rent and utilities. Part
    of her knows that she would be able to live on her own, but another part wonders
    if she could. For the time being, her bills are paid by the retirement funds
    of the golden girls that need drink refills every Friday \u201Cnight.\u201D"
